API ENDPOINTS

  PAID APIs (x402 protected — requires X-Payment header)
    GET  /api/v1/catalog          List all active on-chain APIs with prices
    GET  /api/v1/call/:apiId      Universal paid entry point — proxies any registered API
    GET  /api/v1/internal/:key    Unauthenticated data handlers for built-in feeds
                                  (btc, eth, sol, gas — called by the proxy, not agents directly)

  PAYMENT
    GET  /payment/nonce           Generate fresh nonce + deadline (5 min expiry)
    POST /payment/verify          Pre-flight signature check (no nonce consumed)
    GET  /payment/balance/:addr   USDC balance for any wallet
    GET  /payment/status          Payment layer health check

  REGISTRY (on-chain APIRegistry.sol, merged with off-chain metadata)
    GET  /registry/apis                  List all APIs — on-chain + metadata merged
                                         Query params: ?category=Crypto/DeFi  ?active=true
    GET  /registry/api/:id               Single API detail — full on-chain + metadata
    GET  /registry/slug/:slug            Resolve a URL slug to full API detail
    GET  /registry/provider/:addr        All APIs owned by a provider
    GET  /registry/categories            Distinct categories (marketplace filter bar)
    GET  /registry/stats                 Total API count + chain status
    POST /registry/register              Register a new API on-chain
    PUT  /registry/api/:id               Update price or active status

  METADATA (off-chain, Supabase — requires SUPABASE_* env vars)
    POST /registry/metadata/:id          Submit or update rich metadata for an API
                                         Header: X-Provider-Address (ownership check)
                                         Body: { slug, category, tags, description,
                                                 longDesc, params, codeExample,
                                                 responseSchema }
    GET  /registry/metadata/:id          Fetch metadata for a single API

  FAUCET (testnet only)
    GET  /faucet/status/:address  Check cooldown and USDC balance for a wallet
    POST /faucet/mint             Mint 1000 MockUSDC to a wallet (1h cooldown)

  DASHBOARD (wallet spend view)
    GET  /dashboard/:address              Overview: balance, spend, call count
    GET  /dashboard/:address/history      Paginated call history
    GET  /dashboard/:address/spend        Spend breakdown per API

  PROVIDER PORTAL (earnings view)
    GET  /provider/:address               Overview: earnings, APIs, call stats
    GET  /provider/:address/earnings      Earnings breakdown per API
    GET  /provider/:address/calls         Paginated incoming call history

  UTILITY
    GET  /                        Health check + full endpoint map
    GET  /config                  Public config for agent onboarding
                                  (contract addresses, network, quickstart steps)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
METADATA SYSTEM

  The on-chain APIRegistry stores only trust-critical fields:
    provider, name, endpoint, pricePerCall, active

  Rich discovery and docs fields are stored off-chain in Supabase, keyed by apiId:
    slug, category, tags, description, longDesc,
    params, codeExample, responseSchema

  This split keeps gas costs low while giving the marketplace full API docs.
  The metadata service degrades gracefully — if Supabase is not configured,
  all registry endpoints still work, returning null for metadata fields.

  Supabase table: api_metadata
    api_id          text PRIMARY KEY
    slug            text UNIQUE
    category        text
    tags            text[]
    description     text
    long_desc       text
    params          jsonb   -- [{ name, type, required, description }]
    code_example    text
    response_schema text
    created_at      timestamptz
    updated_at      timestamptz

  SQL to create the table is in src/services/metadata.service.ts (header comment).

  Typical provider flow after on-chain registration:
    1. POST /registry/register  →  get apiId
    2. POST /registry/metadata/:apiId  →  submit docs, category, slug
    3. GET  /registry/apis  →  API appears in marketplace with full metadata
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
X402 PAYMENT FLOW

    Agent                    Gateway                  Morph Hoodi
      |                         |                          |
      |-- GET /api/v1/btc ----->|                          |
      |<-- 402 Payment Required-|                          |
      |    (amount, provider,   |                          |
      |     facilitator,        |                          |
      |     chainId, nonce URL) |                          |
      |                         |                          |
      |-- GET /payment/nonce -->|                          |
      |<-- { nonce, deadline } -|                          |
      |                         |                          |
      | [agent signs off-chain] |                          |
      |                         |                          |
      |-- GET /api/v1/btc ----->|                          |
      |   X-Payment: base64(    |                          |
      |     payer, provider,    |                          |
      |     amount, nonce,      |-- verifyPayment()        |
      |     deadline, sig)      |   (off-chain ECDSA)      |
      |                         |                          |
      |<-- 200 OK + data -------|                          |
      |                         |-- facilitator.settle() ->|
      |                         |   (payer, provider, sig) |
      |                         |                          |-- verify sig == payer
      |                         |                          |-- transferFrom(payer->provider)
      |                         |                          |-- emit PaymentSettled
      |                         |<-- txHash ---------------|
      |                         |   ledger.record()        |

    Key properties:
    - Agent signs once, gateway settles on-chain
    - Nonce consumed in-memory before response, permanently on-chain after settle
    - Settlement is async — agent does not wait for on-chain confirmation
    - Ledger is rebuilt from chain events on server restart (replayLedgerFromChain)
    - Every settled payment is recorded in the ledger for dashboard queries
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SERVICES

    blockchain.service.ts
        Wraps all on-chain interactions: signature verification, settlement,
        APIRegistry read/write, USDC balance queries, ledger replay from chain.
        Built-in feeds are registered as real on-chain entries at startup.

    metadata.service.ts
        Supabase-backed CRUD for off-chain API metadata. Initialised at startup.
        Degrades gracefully if SUPABASE_* env vars are not set.

    ledger.service.ts
        In-memory payment history. Rebuilt from PaymentSettled chain events on
        restart. Capped at 1000 entries. Serves dashboard and provider portal.

    nonce.service.ts
        In-memory nonce store (first line of replay protection, 24h TTL).
        The X402Facilitator on-chain usedNonces mapping is the permanent truth.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCRIPTS
    node scripts/pay.mjs      Single end-to-end payment test (BTC endpoint)
    node scripts/agent.mjs    Full demo agent (multi-call autonomous simulation)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SMART CONTRACTS

    APIRegistry.sol
        - Permissionless API registration
        - On-chain pricing (pricePerCall in USDC, 6 decimals)
        - Provider ownership and update rights
        - Enumerable listings for agent discovery

    X402Facilitator.sol
        - Gateway-mediated settlement
        - ECDSA signature verification against declared payer
        - Nonce-based replay protection
        - 99% to provider / 1% to treasury fee split
        - Deadline enforcement

    MockUSDC.sol
        - ERC-20 test token (6 decimals, matches mainnet USDC)
        - Faucet: 1000 USDC per mint, 1h cooldown per wallet
        - Used by the /faucet endpoints
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROJECT STRUCTURE

    src/
      server.ts                 Express app, bootstrap, route mounting
      middleware/
        x402.middleware.ts      Payment-as-auth middleware (402 / verify / settle)
      routes/
        api.routes.ts           Paid API endpoints + generic proxy
        registry.routes.ts      On-chain registry + metadata merge
        metadata.routes.ts      Off-chain metadata CRUD (Supabase)
        payment.routes.ts       Nonce, verify, balance, status
        dashboard.routes.ts     Wallet spend analytics
        provider.routes.ts      Provider earnings analytics
        faucet.routes.ts        MockUSDC testnet faucet
      services/
        blockchain.service.ts   All on-chain interactions (ethers v6)
        metadata.service.ts     Off-chain metadata (Supabase)
        ledger.service.ts       In-memory payment history
        nonce.service.ts        In-memory nonce replay protection
    scripts/
      pay.mjs                   Single payment test script
      agent.mjs                 Demo autonomous agent
